{"text":"kuruntokai","n":119,"lines":["சிறுவெள் ளரவின் அவ்வரிக் குருளை","கான யானை அணங்கி யாஅங்கு","இளையள் முளைவாள் எயிற்றள்","வளையுடைக் கையள்எம் அணங்கி யோளே"],"tr":["ciṟuveḷ ḷaraviṉ avvarik kuruḷai","kāṉa yāṉai aṇaṅki yāaṅku","iḷaiyaḷ muḷaivāḷ eyiṟṟaḷ","vaḷaiyuṭaik kaiyaḷem aṇaṅki yōḷē"],"colophon":{"tinai":"kuṟiñci","tinai_ta":"குறிஞ்சி","speaker_ta":"தலைவன் கூற்று","poet_ta":"சத்திநாதனார்","speaker_en":"the hero (talaivaṉ)","poet_tr":"Cattinātaṉār"},"scan":{"meter":"nēricai āciriyappā","ok":true,"checks":[{"name":"lines","ok":true,"detail":"4 lines"},{"name":"feet per line","ok":true,"detail":"3×4, 1×3 feet"},{"name":"foot types","ok":true,"detail":"iyaṟcīr 13, veṇcīr 2"},{"name":"linkage","ok":true,"detail":"veṇṭaḷai 6, āciriyattaḷai 6, kalittaḷai 2"},{"name":"ending","ok":true,"detail":"ends on ஏ"}],"ending":"ஏ","lines":[[{"text":"சிறுவெள்","tr":"ciṟuveḷ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"சிறு","tr":"ciṟu"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வெள்","tr":"veḷ"}]},{"text":"ளரவின்","tr":"ḷaraviṉ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"ளர","tr":"ḷara"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வின்","tr":"viṉ"}]},{"text":"அவ்வரிக்","tr":"avvarik","foot":"kūviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"அவ்","tr":"av"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"வரிக்","tr":"varik"}]},{"text":"குருளை","tr":"kuruḷai","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"குரு","tr":"kuru"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளை","tr":"ḷai"}]}],[{"text":"கான","tr":"kāṉa","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"கா","tr":"kā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ன","tr":"ṉa"}]},{"text":"யானை","tr":"yāṉai","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யா","tr":"yā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"னை","tr":"ṉai"}]},{"text":"அணங்கி","tr":"aṇaṅki","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"அணங்","tr":"aṇaṅ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கி","tr":"ki"}]},{"text":"யாஅங்கு","tr":"yāaṅku","foot":"tēmāṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யா","tr":"yā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"அங்","tr":"aṅ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கு","tr":"ku"}]}],[{"text":"இளையள்","tr":"iḷaiyaḷ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"இளை","tr":"iḷai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யள்","tr":"yaḷ"}]},{"text":"முளைவாள்","tr":"muḷaivāḷ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"முளை","tr":"muḷai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வாள்","tr":"vāḷ"}]},{"text":"எயிற்றள்","tr":"eyiṟṟaḷ","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"எயிற்","tr":"eyiṟ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றள்","tr":"ṟaḷ"}]}],[{"text":"வளையுடைக்","tr":"vaḷaiyuṭaik","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"வளை","tr":"vaḷai"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"யுடைக்","tr":"yuṭaik"}]},{"text":"கையள்எம்","tr":"kaiyaḷem","foot":"tēmāṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"கை","tr":"kai"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யள்","tr":"yaḷ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"எம்","tr":"em"}]},{"text":"அணங்கி","tr":"aṇaṅki","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"அணங்","tr":"aṇaṅ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"கி","tr":"ki"}]},{"text":"யோளே","tr":"yōḷē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யோ","tr":"yō"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளே","tr":"ḷē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"சிறு","parts":[{"text":"சிறு","lemma":"சிறுமை","gloss":"small"}],"gloss":"small"},{"surface":"வெள்","parts":[{"text":"வெள்","lemma":"வெண்மை","gloss":"white"}],"gloss":"white"},{"surface":"அரவின்","parts":[{"text":"அரவு","lemma":"அரவு","gloss":"snake"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the snake"},{"surface":"அவ்வரி","parts":[{"text":"அவ்வரி","lemma":"அவ்வரி","gloss":"beautiful stripes"}],"gloss":"beautiful stripes","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"குருளை","parts":[{"text":"குருளை","lemma":"குருளை","gloss":"young one"}],"gloss":"young one"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கான","parts":[{"text":"கான்","lemma":"கான்","gloss":"forest"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"of the forest"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"அணங்கி","parts":[{"text":"அணங்கு","lemma":"அணங்கு","gloss":"afflict"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"having (verbal participle suffix)"}],"gloss":"having afflicted"},{"surface":"யாஅங்கு","parts":[{"text":"யாஅங்கு","lemma":"யாங்கு","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இளையள்","parts":[{"text":"இளை","lemma":"இளமை","gloss":"young"},{"text":"அள்","lemma":"அள்","gloss":"she"}],"gloss":"she who is young"},{"surface":"முளை","parts":[{"text":"முளை","lemma":"முளை","gloss":"sprout"}],"gloss":"sprout"},{"surface":"வாள்","parts":[{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"வாள்","gloss":"bright"}],"gloss":"bright"},{"surface":"எயிற்றள்","parts":[{"text":"எயிற்று","lemma":"எயிறு","gloss":"tooth"},{"text":"அள்","lemma":"அள்","gloss":"she"}],"gloss":"she of the teeth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வளை","parts":[{"text":"வளை","lemma":"வளை","gloss":"bangle"}],"gloss":"bangle"},{"surface":"உடை","parts":[{"text":"உடை","lemma":"உடை","gloss":"possessing"}],"gloss":"possessing"},{"surface":"கையள்","parts":[{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"hand"},{"text":"அள்","lemma":"அள்","gloss":"she"}],"gloss":"she of the hands"},{"surface":"எம்","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"me"}],"gloss":"me"},{"surface":"அணங்கியோளே","parts":[{"text":"அணங்கு","lemma":"அணங்கு","gloss":"torment"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"ஓள்","lemma":"ஓள்","gloss":"she"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"she who tormented me indeed"}]}],"literal":"The beautiful-striped young pup of a small white snake / having afflicted a forest elephant, in that manner / she who is young, she of the sprout-like bright teeth, / she of the bangled hands, has afflicted me.","translation":"Just as the young pup of a small, white, beautifully-striped snake torments a massive forest elephant, so has she—young, with bright, sprout-like teeth and bangled hands—tormented me.","modern":"ஒரு சிறிய, வெண்மையான, அழகிய வரிகளையுடைய பாம்பின் குட்டியானது காட்டில் வாழும் பெரிய யானையை வருத்துவது போல, இளமையானவளும், முளை போன்ற ஒளிரும் பற்களை உடையவளும், வளையல்களை அணிந்த கைகளை உடையவளுமாகிய அவள் என்னை வருத்தினாள்.","explanation":"This poem is set in the Kuriñci (mountainous) landscape, where the theme is the union of lovers and the intense feelings of first love. The speaker is the hero, who has just met the heroine and is overwhelmed by her beauty and the power she holds over him. He compares himself to a mighty forest elephant and the heroine to a tiny, young, beautifully striped white snake. Just as a small snake's presence can completely paralyze and distress a giant elephant, this young, delicate girl with bright, sprout-like teeth and bangled hands has completely captivated and tormented his heart. The contrast between the smallness of the snake and the greatness of the elephant highlights the overwhelming power of love. Key words include 'அணங்கி' (having afflicted) and 'குருளை' (young pup).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.6],[0.6,1.5],[1.5,1.7],[1.7,2.6],[2.6,2.7],[2.7,3.0],[3.13,3.8],[4.17,4.8],[4.8,5.6],[5.6,5.8],[5.8,5.98],[5.98,6.16],[6.16,6.87],[6.87,7.94]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.67,0.8],[0.8,1.5],[1.67,2.0],[2.0,2.9],[2.9,3.0],[3.0,3.3],[3.3,4.4],[4.4,5.13],[5.13,5.13],[5.13,7.33],[7.33,7.33],[7.33,8.8],[8.8,9.3],[9.3,9.4]]}}